==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|machinatus}}, past participle of {{m|la|machinor||to contrive, plan, devise, plot, scheme}}, from {{m|la|machina||a machine, contrivance, device, scheme}}; see [[machine]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmækɪneɪt/|/ˈmæʃɪneɪt/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|machinat}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[devise]] a [[plot]] or [[secret]] [[plan]]; to [[conspire]].
#* '''2011''', Ian Douglas Robertson, ''Turtle Hawks''
#*: Had she already managed to '''machinate''' a cushy job for her husband?

